@startuml naive_antipattern
autonumber
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam boxPadding 10
skinparam participantPadding 15

actor "Client\n(Naive Step-Up)" as Client
box "iron-mcp Server (:5302)" #F8F9FA
    participant "McpAuthServer\n(Resource Server)" as RS
end box
box "Keycloak on danarch (:10000)" #E8F4F8
    participant "Keycloak AS\n(Stateless Grants)" as AS
end box

== Initial State ==
note over Client
  heldToken = token_1 (scope="mcp:read")
end note

Client -> RS: POST /mcp (token_1): tools/call export_full_data
RS --> Client: 403 Forbidden\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_scope",\n  scope="mcp:read mcp:export"

== The Anti-Pattern: Requesting ONLY Missing Scopes ==
note over Client #FADBD8
  THE NAIVE MISTAKE:
  Assumes grants accumulate at the AS.
  missing = challenged \ granted = { "mcp:export" }
  Client requests ONLY "mcp:export"!
end note

Client -> AS: POST /token\nscope=mcp:export
AS --> Client: 200 OK\n{\n  "access_token": "token_naive",\n  "scope": "mcp:export"\n}
note over AS
  The AS is STATELESS:
  A re-authorization REPLACES the token!
  "mcp:read" was omitted from the request, so it is GONE!
end note

== Damage 1: Retry Still Fails ==
Client -> RS: POST /mcp (token_naive): tools/call export_full_data
RS -> RS: Check scopes: 'export_full_data' requires ["mcp:read", "mcp:export"]\nToken grants only ["mcp:export"] -> STILL MISSING mcp:read!
RS --> Client: 403 Forbidden\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_scope", scope="mcp:read mcp:export"

== Damage 2: Regression in Previously Working Tool ==
Client -> RS: POST /mcp (token_naive): tools/call read_summary
RS -> RS: Check scopes: 'read_summary' requires ["mcp:read"]\nToken grants only ["mcp:export"] -> FAILS!
RS --> Client: 403 Forbidden\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_scope", scope="mcp:read"
note over Client #FDEDEC
  PRODUCTION NIGHTMARE:
  A tool that worked perfectly 5 seconds ago now fails.
  The regression surfaces far from the code that triggered it.
end note
@enduml
